Build1=FLAG_SECURE,net.gdmeunier.pinunblocker
Build2=NO_FLAG_SECURE,net.gdmeunier.pinunblocker,NO_FLAG_SECURE
File1=About.png
File2=Base.bal
File3=Main.bal
File4=Scan.bal
File5=USB.png
FileGroup1=Icons
FileGroup2=Layouts
FileGroup3=Layouts
FileGroup4=Layouts
FileGroup5=Icons
Group=Activities
Library1=core
Library2=javaobject
Library3=lightruntimepermissions
Library4=threading
Library5=newqrcodereaderview
ManifestCode='~\n~'Android PIN Unblocker's application manifest file~\n~'~\n~~\n~'This application supports Android 2.3.2 and higher (API level 9+)~\n~'This application guarantees compliance with Android up to Android 13 (API level 33)~\n~'~\n~'This application requires atleast Android 2.3.2 (API level 9) for:~\n~' - Camera-related functions~\n~'~\n~AddManifestText(<uses-sdk android:minSdkVersion="9" android:targetSdkVersion="33" />)~\n~~\n~'This application makes use of Camera hardware and Flashlight~\n~'However this is not strictly required to run this application~\n~'~\n~'Features used for:~\n~' - Scanning QR codes~\n~'~\n~AddManifestText(~\n~<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.camera"           android:required="false" />~\n~<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.camera.front"     android:required="false" />~\n~<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.camera.any"       android:required="false" />~\n~<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.camera.autofocus" android:required="false" />~\n~<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.camera.flash"     android:required="false" />)~\n~~\n~'This application makes use of USB-OTG (On-The-Go)~\n~'However this is not strictly required to run this application~\n~'~\n~'Feature used for:~\n~' - Unblocking smartcards over USB~\n~'~\n~AddManifestText(~\n~<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.usb.host"         android:required="false" />)~\n~~\n~'This application supports all screen sizes & densities~\n~AddManifestText(~\n~<supports-screens android:smallScreens="true"~\n~                  android:normalScreens="true"~\n~                  android:largeScreens="true"~\n~                  android:xlargeScreens="true"~\n~                  android:anyDensity="true" />)~\n~~\n~'This application cans broadcast Intents:~\n~' - Opening HTTP or HTTPS links~\n~'~\n~'This requirement was introduced starting with Android 11 (API level 30)~\n~AddManifestText(~\n~<queries>~\n~    <intent>~\n~        <action   android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW" />~\n~        <category android:name="android.intent.category.BROWSABLE" />~\n~        <data android:scheme="https" />~\n~        <data android:scheme="http" />~\n~    </intent>~\n~</queries>)~\n~~\n~'~\n~'Camera and Flashlight permissions are automatically inserted when using~\n~'the NewQRCodeReaderView library~\n~'~\n~~\n~'Application identity (automatically inserted)~\n~SetApplicationAttribute(android:label, "$LABEL$")~\n~~\n~'Application icon (uses a mipmap instead of a drawable)~\n~SetApplicationAttribute(android:icon, "@mipmap/ic_launcher")~\n~~\n~'Application theme (this app uses a custom theme)~\n~SetApplicationAttribute(android:theme, "@style/AppTheme")~\n~~\n~'Application's task affinity (this application refuses to share affinity with other ones):~\n~' - Always detach this application's Activities from the task stack of other apps~\n~' - We do this by clearing its task affinity attribute (setting it to "")~\n~'~\n~'This attribute cans be set for either in <activity /> or <application /> tags~\n~' - Setting it for the <application /> covers all Activities~\n~'~\n~'This is done for security reasons, so that other applications cannot do~\n~'task reparenting attacks on it (known as StrandHogg vulnerability)~\n~SetApplicationAttribute("android:taskAffinity", "")~\n~~\n~'This application wishes to benefit from hardware acceleration:~\n~' - Performance optimization for the Camera preview (QR code scanning)~\n~'~\n~'This attribute cans be set for either in <activity /> or <application /> tags~\n~' - Setting it for the <application /> tag covers all Activities~\n~'~\n~'We wish to benefit from it for all this application's Activities~\n~SetApplicationAttribute(android:hardwareAccelerated, "true")~\n~~\n~'The running state of this application should never be preserved across reboots:~\n~' - Don't let Android persist this application's state across device reboots and on shutdown~\n~' - We don't want the user having leftovers (forensic traces) from Activities across reboots~\n~'~\n~'This attribute was introduced starting with Android 5.0 (API level 21)~\n~'~\n~'Add all this application's Activities here~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:persistableMode", "persistNever")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:persistableMode", "persistNever")~\n~~\n~'This application's Activities when started by a specific user,~\n~'should only be visible for this user and other ones on the device:~\n~' - We don't want to let one Android user launch one of this application's Activities,~\n~'   then have other Android users on the same device being able to see~\n~'   this user's own Activities in their task history (for security reasons)~\n~'~\n~' - Each Android user account on a device should~\n~'   launch their own Activities if they want to~\n~'   see those in their own task histories~\n~'~\n~'This attribute was introduced starting with Android 6 (API level 23)~\n~'~\n~'Add all this application's Activities here~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:showForAllUsers", "false")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:showForAllUsers", "false")~\n~~\n~'Mark the Main Activity as exported~\n~'~\n~'Newer versions of Android require that Activities with <intent-filters /> must~\n~'explicitly be marked as exported for security reasons~\n~'~\n~'This requirement was introduced starting with Android 12 (API level 32)~\n~'~\n~'Set it for Activities that can receive Intents in this application~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:exported", "true")~\n~~\n~'Mark the Scan Activity as unexported (private):~\n~' - Android applications should always mark as unexported all Activities that~\n~'   are not explicitly made open to other ones~\n~'~\n~'We mark all Activities that are not explicitly callable from other applications as~\n~'unexported for security reasons (as a security precaution)~\n~'~\n~'Set it for all Activities that you don't wish to explicitly offer to other applications~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:exported", "false")~\n~~\n~'Exclude the Scan Activity from the Android Recent Apps panel:~\n~' - Only the Main Activity (entry point) should appear in it~\n~'~\n~'Add all Activities other than the Main one here~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:excludeFromRecents", "true")~\n~~\n~'Make the Main Activity automatically disappear form the Recent Apps panel when finished:~\n~' - This Activity will only be visible until the user intentionally exits the application,~\n~'   then it will disappear from the Recent Apps panel to avoid leaving traces of use~\n~'~\n~'This attribute was introduced starting with Android 5.0 (API level 21)~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:autoRemoveFromRecents", "true")~\n~~\n~'Set the Main Activity's launch mode to singleTop:~\n~' - Atleast a singleTop or singleTask launch mode is required to receive~\n~'   onNewIntent Activity callbacks~\n~'~\n~'Attribute used for:~\n~' - Receiving Admin key texts shared to this application~\n~'~\n~'Set it for Activities that can receive Intents in this application~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:launchMode", "singleTop")~\n~~\n~'Enforce stricter Intent matching rules for sending Intents to the Main Activity:~\n~' - Explicit Intents must match this application's exact component name~\n~' - Intents without any ACTION type don't match this application~\n~'~\n~'This attribute cans be set for either in <activity /> or <application /> tags~\n~' - Setting it for the <application /> tag covers all Activities~\n~'~\n~'This attribute was introduced starting with Android 16 (API level 36)~\n~'~\n~'Set it for Activities that can receive Intents in this application~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:intentMatchingFlags", "enforceIntentFilter")~\n~~\n~'Add a Share To Intent filter to the Main Activity:~\n~' - Allow sharing Admin key texts from other applications to this one~\n~'~\n~'Used attributes:~\n~' - "android:autoVerify": Introduced starting with Android 6 (API level 23)~\n~'~\n~'                         It's some useless thing that's used for verifying~\n~'                         Digital Asset Links JSON files on remote websites~\n~'~\n~' - "android:order":      Introduced starting with Android 9 (API level 28)~\n~'~\n~'                         This is the priority order of Intent filters~\n~'                         The higher the number the higher the priority~\n~'~\n~'                         It only sets the priority of this application's own~\n~'                         Intent filters~\n~'~\n~'Note:~\n~' - I don't want to use the "android:priority" Intent filter attribute since it would~\n~'   interfere with other applications' own Intent filter offers, by taking priority over~\n~'   their own offers when you want to share text to a different application instead of this one~\n~'~\n~' - So out of courtesy for other applications, we only use the "android:order" Intent filter attribute~\n~'   instead of the "android:priority" one~\n~'~\n~AddActivityText(Main,~\n~<intent-filter android:label="Share Admin Key"~\n~               android:autoVerify="false"~\n~               android:order="1">~\n~	<action   android:name="android.intent.action.SEND" />~\n~	<category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />~\n~	<data     android:mimeType="text/plain" />~\n~</intent-filter>)~\n~~\n~'Mark Picture-in-Picture mode (PiP) as unsupported:~\n~' - we don't want to support it for security reasons~\n~'~\n~'Add all this application's Activities here~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:supportsPictureInPicture", "false")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:supportsPictureInPicture", "false")~\n~~\n~'Ask the connected display not to perform graphical post-processing for~\n~'this application (minimal post-processing):~\n~' - Some new-technology displays might try to improve the graphics and colors of this application,~\n~'   but we don't need any such graphical enhancements here~\n~'~\n~'This attribute was introduced starting with Android 11 (API level 30)~\n~'~\n~'Add all this application's Activities here~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:preferMinimalPostProcessing", "true")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:preferMinimalPostProcessing", "true")~\n~~\n~'Opt-out of predictive animations in this application's Activities:~\n~' - We don't use any animations in this application for performance reasons,~\n~'   because we just don't need fancy animations in a technical application~\n~'~\n~'Add all this application's Activities here~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback", "false")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback", "false")~\n~~\n~~\n~'Intercept mundane device configuration change events to deliberately ignore them:~\n~' - Tell Android that we will handle these configuration change events, but we will actually~\n~'   simply ignore them, so that Android doesn't destroy then re-create this application's Activities for~\n~'   mundane device configuration changes that are not even related to the device display or its orientation~\n~'~\n~'Real display-related configuration change events are:~\n~' - orientation~\n~' - screenSize~\n~' - smallestScreenSize~\n~'~\n~'So we hook all the other ones to simply ignore them~\n~'~\n~'Add all this application's Activities here~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:configChanges", "colorMode|grammaticalGender|keyboard|keyboardHidden|locale|mcc|mnc|navigation|touchscreen")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:configChanges", "colorMode|grammaticalGender|keyboard|keyboardHidden|locale|mcc|mnc|navigation|touchscreen")~\n~~\n~'Tell Android that it cans shrink our application's Activities if necessary:~\n~' - When it shows the keyboard, the keyboard should not cover Activity content~\n~' - This attribute tells Android that it cans adjust the Activity pan if necessary~\n~'~\n~'The "adjustPan" part is the important one, which should not be needed to set explicitly,~\n~'but Basic4Android explicitly sets by default a windowSoftInputMode value of "stateHidden"~\n~'~\n~'So we have to override Basic4Android's default value with our own instead~\n~'~\n~'We also want to prevent Android from automatically setting~\n~'the focus on the first Activity UI element on application resume,~\n~'because we already handle this on our own in our ViewState management functions~\n~'~\n~'So we also use "stateAlwaysHidden" too instead of just using "stateHidden":~\n~' - "By default, Android will automatically assign initial focus~\n~'    to the first EditText or focusable control in your Activity.~\n~'	 [...]~\n~'    The windowSoftInputMode attribute in AndroidManifest.xml,~\n~'    when set to stateAlwaysHidden, instructs the keyboard to~\n~'    ignore this automatically-assigned initial focus.~\n~'    [...]~\n~'    Therefore, stateAlwaysHidden is VERY poorly named indeed.~\n~'    It should perhaps be called ignoreInitialFocus instead."~\n~'~\n~'Add all Activities that contain input fields here~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:windowSoftInputMode", "adjustPan|stateAlwaysHidden")~\n~~\n~'----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- -----~\n~~\n~'~\n~'This part is for creating the application's resources~\n~'~\n~~\n~'~\n~' - Application themes -~\n~'~\n~~\n~'Android 8.0+ -> DeviceDefault parent theme~\n~CreateResource(values-v26, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV26" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV26" parent="@android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault">~\n~		<item name="android:windowBackground">@color/MyWindowBackground</item>~\n~		<item name="android:editTextStyle">@style/MyEditTextStyleV26</item>~\n~		<item name="android:windowShowWallpaper">false</item>~\n~		<item name="android:windowActivityTransitions">false</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~	<style name="MyEditTextStyleV26" parent="@style/MyEditTextStyleV23">~\n~		<item name="android:imeOptions">flagNoExtractUi|flagNoFullscreen|flagNoPersonalizedLearning</item>~\n~		<item name="android:importantForAutofill">noExcludeDescendants</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 6-7.1~\n~CreateResource(values-v23, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV23" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV23" parent="@style/MyThemeV21">~\n~		<item name="android:editTextStyle">@style/MyEditTextStyleV23</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~	<style name="MyEditTextStyleV23" parent="@style/MyEditTextStyleV11">~\n~		<item name="android:allowUndo">false</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 5.0-5.1.1 -> Material parent theme~\n~CreateResource(values-v21, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV21" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV21" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material">~\n~		<item name="android:windowBackground">@color/MyWindowBackground</item>~\n~		<item name="android:editTextStyle">@style/MyEditTextStyleV11</item>~\n~		<item name="android:windowShowWallpaper">false</item>~\n~		<item name="android:windowActivityTransitions">false</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 3.0-4.4.4 -> Holo parent theme~\n~CreateResource(values-v11, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV11" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV11" parent="@android:style/Theme.Holo">~\n~		<item name="android:windowBackground">@color/MyWindowBackground</item>~\n~		<item name="android:editTextStyle">@style/MyEditTextStyleV11</item>~\n~		<item name="android:windowShowWallpaper">false</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~	<style name="MyEditTextStyleV11" parent="@style/MyEditTextStyleV5">~\n~		<item name="android:imeOptions">flagNoExtractUi|flagNoFullscreen</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 2.3.3-2.3.7~\n~CreateResource(values-v10, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV10" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV10" parent="@style/MyThemeV5">~\n~		<item name="android:windowShowWallpaper">false</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 2.0-2.3.2~\n~CreateResource(values-v5, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV5" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV5" parent="@style/MyThemeV3">~\n~		<item name="android:editTextStyle">@style/MyEditTextStyleV5</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~	<style name="MyEditTextStyleV5" parent="@style/MyEditTextStyleV3">~\n~		<item name="android:inputType">textVisiblePassword|textNoSuggestions</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 1.5-1.6~\n~CreateResource(values-v3, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV3" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV3" parent="@style/MyTheme">~\n~		<item name="android:editTextStyle">@style/MyEditTextStyleV3</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~	<style name="MyEditTextStyleV3" parent="@android:style/Widget.EditText">~\n~		<item name="android:inputType">textVisiblePassword</item>~\n~		<item name="android:imeOptions">flagNoExtractUi</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 1.0-1.1 -> Theme parent theme~\n~CreateResource(values, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyTheme" />~\n~	<style name="MyTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme">~\n~		<item name="android:windowBackground">@color/MyWindowBackground</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'~\n~' - Default Activity & application colors -~\n~'~\n~~\n~'Android version doesn't matter (all versions need to pick the same color)~\n~CreateResource(values, colors.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<color name="MyWindowBackground">#1C1C1C</color>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~~\n~
Module1=MyAdvanced
Module10=Scan
Module11=Smartcard
Module2=MyCCID
Module3=MyCommon
Module4=MyConstants
Module5=MyCryptography
Module6=MyLifecycleTracking
Module7=MySecurity
Module8=MySmartcardReader
Module9=MySynchronousSleep
NumberOfFiles=5
NumberOfLibraries=5
NumberOfModules=11
Version=12.5
@EndOfDesignText@

#Region Project Attributes 
	#ApplicationLabel: Android PIN Unblocker
	#VersionCode: 70
	#VersionName: 5.0.0
	
	'SupportedOrientations possible values: unspecified, landscape or portrait.
	#SupportedOrientations: unspecified
	
	'We don't want to allow installing this application on external storage:
	' - The user might otherwisse install it on their external storage,
	'   then lose access to the application when they remove it from their device
	'
	#CanInstallToExternalStorage: False
	
	#BridgeLogger: False
	#MultiDex:     False
	
	'Keystore used for signing the application
	'You can also use your own keystore file
	'
	'The keystore password is also used for unlock the selected key inside
	'the keystore as well, so make sure that both passwords are the same
	'(keystore + specific key's) when using your own one
	'
	'The Working Directory of all project options and custom build actions is always
	'the "Objects" folder, just so you know about it
	#SignKeyFile:      "..\Keystore\debug.keystore"
	#SignKeyAlgorithm: -digestalg SHA1 -sigalg SHA256withRSA
	#SignKeyAlias:     androiddebugkey
	#SignKeyPassword:  android
	
#End Region

#Region Activity Attributes 
	#FullScreen:   False
	#IncludeTitle: True
	
#End Region

#Region Module File Attributes
	'Ignore "The recommended value for android:targetSdkVersion is x (manifest editor)" warning (#31)
	'Ignore "This sub should only be used for variables declaration or assignments of primitive values" warning (#29)
	#IgnoreWarnings: 31,29
	
#End Region

#Region Project Macros
	'Replace the full icon fonts with trimmed ones:
	' - These specific fonts are also now required for unofficial custom glyph additions,
	'   such as the copyleft glyph (but also any future ones)
	'
	' - The default working directory is the "Objects" folder
	'
	'Robocopy switches:
	' - /MT: multi-threaded copy mode
	' - /E:  include (copy) subfolders and also the empty ones
	' - /IT: include (replace) tweaked files (not same file attributes)
	' - /IS: include (replace) same files
	'
	#CustomBuildAction: folders ready, %WINDIR%\System32\robocopy.exe, "..\Fonts" ".\bin\extra\assets" /MT /E /IT /IS
	
	'Set the application icon using a mipmap resource
	'
	'The contents of this folder will be copied to the temporary
	'build diretory's "res" folder
	'
	'You can use multiple #AdditionalRes directives
	#AdditionalRes: ../Icons
	
	'Remove Basic4Android's automatically added "icon.png" file
	'in the Objects folder's "res" directory:
	' - We use a mipmap now instead of a drawable,
	'   so our new icon file will be stored inside a "mipmap" folder
	'
	' - However Basic4Android will mistakenly belive that our application
	'   has no icon, and will autoamtically try adding one (default B4X icon)
	'
	'So we use a #CustomBuildAction macro that automatically deletes it
	'before Basic4Android compiles the resources of our application
	'
	'The default working directory is the "Objects" folder
	'
	'cmd switches:
	' - /c: provide an inline command (necessary or you have to provide a batch file)
	'
	' - DEL: delete a file or folder
	'   - /F: delete the file or folder even if set to read-only
	'   - /Q: quiet mode (no confirmation before deletion)
	'
	' - & exit 0: always return exit code 0 (success) even if deleting the file fails,
	'             such as if the file is already deleted prior
	'
	#CustomBuildAction: folders ready, %WINDIR%\System32\cmd.exe, /c DEL ".\res\drawable\icon.png" /F /Q & exit 0
	
#End Region

'----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- -----

'
'Java native code
'

#If Java

private String activityName = "main";

private myadvanced myadvancedInstance = new myadvanced();

